<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 250 0 R
/T (Power cardio is training for explosive Power. Training for Power is similiar to training for Speed, we try to lift very fast. However, when we train for speed we lift as fast as we can with no resistance \(weights\) to slow us down. Training for Explosive Power means we lift as fast as we can but against load \(WITH moderate weights.\) )
/E (Power cardio is training for explosive Power. Training for Power is similiar to training for Speed, we try to lift very fast. However, when we train for speed we lift as fast as we can with no resistance \(weights\) to slow us down. Training for Explosive Power means we lift as fast as we can but against load \(WITH moderate weights.\) )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
